BUILD: sfvictorian-opus: a San Francisco Victorian single-family home (an Italianate or Queen Anne "painted lady"), on a narrow, deep city lot on a sloping street. Recognisable elements: a tall, narrow three-storey front over a garage-level base, with a stair of steps rising to a recessed entry porch with columns; a full-height angled bay window stacked up the front; an elaborate bracketed cornice and a false-front parapet (or a steep front gable with a turret for Queen Anne); tall narrow double-hung windows with ornate pediments and trim; fish-scale shingles and horizontal siding; a painted-lady colour scheme (three or more body and trim colours); a tiny front garden behind an iron fence; party walls close on both sides; a deep back garden with a deck. Inside: an entry hall with a long staircase along the party wall; front parlour behind the bay with a fireplace; dining room; kitchen at the back opening to the garden; upstairs bedrooms front and back, a bathroom with a clawfoot tub; a top-floor room under the roof.
SIZE: about 16 wide (front, x), 50 deep including the front and back gardens, 18 tall from the street; 1:1 scale, a player is 2 blocks tall.
